From 4966af9599c6db203331c360f0c04e65f13a22f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PathOps <noreply@pathops.dev>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:10:02 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] registry: Artifact Store tokens for Application artifact
 identities

PathOps Decision 0061: an Application's artifact ServiceAccount
(<app>-artifact in <app>-ci, capability artifact-store) exchanges its
Kubernetes token at Dex (RFC 8693 through the Kubernetes workload
connector, requested_token_type urn:pathops:params:oauth:token-type:artifact)
for an Artifact Store token: a JWT signed with its own Ed25519 key, with its
own issuer and audience, at most 5 minutes, carrying pathops_application
(the Application id read from the Namespace and ServiceAccount labels, as
for registry tokens) and pathops_operations ["read", "write"].

The registry token issuer is generalized into profiles (section, token
type, ServiceAccount suffix, capability, extra claims): both kinds share
the workload identity checks, the Kubernetes label lookup and the signing.
A build ServiceAccount gets no Artifact Store token and an artifact
ServiceAccount no registry token. Registry tokens are unchanged.

Configuration (opt-in; without it nothing changes):

  artifactTokens:
    clients: [pathops-artifact-store]
    connector: k8s-cell
    issuer: https://dex.example.org/artifacts
    audience: pathops-artifact-store
    signingKeyFile: /etc/dex/artifact/artifact.key
    keyID: artifact-1
    validFor: 5m
